---
import '../../styles/decision.css';
---

<section id="decision" class="decision-section section-pad">
  <div class="container split-grid">
    <div class="section-copy">
      <p class="label muted">Parent pain section</p>
      <h2>A marksheet is not a career map.</h2>
      <p>
        Many students score well, but still remain unclear about which stream actually fits them. Some choose Science
        because friends are choosing it. Some choose Commerce because it feels safer. Some avoid Arts because of
        social pressure, even when their natural strengths point in that direction.
      </p>
      <p>
        The problem is not lack of talent. The problem is making a 40-year career decision using only marks, peer
        pressure and family assumptions.
      </p>
      <ul class="decision-list">
        <li>Your child is in Class 8, 9 or 10.</li>
        <li>You are unsure about Science, Commerce or Arts.</li>
        <li>Your child’s marks do not clearly reveal career direction.</li>
        <li>You and your child are not aligned on career choices.</li>
        <li>Coaching class pressure is influencing the decision.</li>
        <li>You want a calmer, more data-backed way to discuss careers at home.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <figure class="image-card image-card-small">
      <picture>
        <source srcset="/images/parent.webp" type="image/webp" />
        <img src="/images/parent.jpg" alt="Parent and child reviewing study choices together" loading="lazy" width="800" height="598" />
      </picture>
      <figcaption>Guidance before the pressure of stream selection peaks.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
